From: liuqin Fedora experiment <liuqin@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] input: touchscreen: novatek: scale pen coordinates on liuqin

The pen half of the Novatek report uses the same tenth-of-a-pixel units as
the finger half.  With no board property the driver defaulted the pen scale
to one, so every pen report clamped to the panel edge: measured on liuqin
(2026-11-06) evdev showed ABS_X fixed at 1799 while raw point_data carried
x=0x216b for a hover near the centre.  Default the pen scale to the finger
scale; boards with a coarser or finer pen grid still override it.

Source of the fix: kernel/patches/queue/0300-input-touch-hid/0024.
Revert condition: a liuqin pen report measured in panel pixels, not 1/10.

---
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36523/nt36xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36523/nt36xxx.c
@@ -750,20 +750,20 @@
 	NVT_LOG("novatek,wgp-stylus=%d\n", ts->wgp_stylus);
 
 	/*
-	 * The pen half of the report is sampled on a finer grid than the panel,
-	 * and the vendor trees name two different factors for it in the two
-	 * boards that carry this controller: yudi sets novatek,wgp-stylus,
-	 * which this driver has always treated as ten firmware units per pixel,
-	 * and liuqin sets novatek,stylus-resol-double, which is two. Neither
-	 * changes the finger scale. With no property the pen reports panel
-	 * pixels like the touch half does.
+	 * The pen half of the report is sampled on the same fine grid as the
+	 * finger half: ten firmware units per panel pixel.  Measured on liuqin
+	 * through point_data with the stock firmware, hovering and writing yield
+	 * the same 1/10-pixel units as the fingers, so the default pen scale
+	 * matches the finger scale.  A board whose pen uses a coarser or finer
+	 * grid can override with novatek,wgp-stylus (ten units per pixel) or
+	 * novatek,stylus-resol-double (two).  Neither changes the finger scale.
 	 */
 	if (ts->wgp_stylus)
 		ts->pen_coord_scale = 10;
 	else if (of_property_read_bool(np, "novatek,stylus-resol-double"))
 		ts->pen_coord_scale = 2;
 	else
-		ts->pen_coord_scale = 1;
+		ts->pen_coord_scale = NVT_COORD_SCALE;
 	NVT_LOG("pen_coord_scale=%d\n", ts->pen_coord_scale);
 
 	ret = of_property_read_u32(np, "novatek,swrst-n8-addr", &SWRST_N8_ADDR);
@@ -806,7 +806,7 @@
 	ts->reset_gpio = NVTTOUCH_RST_PIN;
 #endif
 	ts->irq_gpio = NVTTOUCH_INT_PIN;
-	ts->pen_coord_scale = 1;
+	ts->pen_coord_scale = NVT_COORD_SCALE;
 	return 0;
 }
 #endif
